# Code: a structure whose rows are taken exactly. Indentation is kept, a bare bar is an empty line,
# and a bar inside a line is only a character. The painter sets it monospaced and highlighted, inside its frame.

scene caption
code fizz python file=fizzbuzz.py | Fizz, then buzz
| def fizzbuzz(n):
|     for i in range(1, n + 1):
|         if i % 15 == 0:
|             print("FizzBuzz")
|         elif i % 3 == 0:
|             print("Fizz")
|         elif i % 5 == 0:
|             print("Buzz")
|         else:
|             print(i)
say | Four branches, one loop. The order of the tests is the whole trick.
wait 2

scene caption
code pipe bash | A pipeline, taken exactly
| # count the words in the three longest files
| wc -w *.md | sort -rn | head -3
|
| echo "done | $(date +%H:%M)"
say aside | The bar in the last line is code, not a table.
wait 2

scene caption
code cfg ts file=config.ts
| export const config = {
|   retries: 3,
|   timeoutMs: 2_500,
| } as const;
say | The same lines, in another language.
wait 2
